Hand-ported, NOT a verbatim upstream patch.

The official series (../amdgpu-hdmi21-vrr-allm/0001-0004) targets AMD's
amd-staging-drm-next branch, which has already split amdgpu_dm.c into separate
amdgpu_dm_connector.c / amdgpu_dm_freesync.c files. That split hasn't landed in
mainline (linux_testing), so those hunks don't apply here. This patch carries the
same logic — HDMI FRL accepted as a FreeSync signal source, VRR capability falling
back to the HF-VSDB when the AMD VSDB doesn't provide a range, VTEM info-packet
transmission on FRL, and ALLM signaling via the HF-VSIF — transplanted into the
equivalent functions still living in amdgpu_dm.c on mainline (parse_hdmi_amd_vsdb's
caller, amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps, update_freesync_state_on_stream,
create_stream_for_sink). One upstream hunk was dropped: a debug-log-only addition
to amdgpu_dm_get_freesync_config_for_crtc, whose mainline equivalent
(update_stream_irq_parameters) doesn't have the connector state / vrefresh
values in scope that the log line needs. No functional behavior was omitted.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
